@wangjunjian/dsh-artifact-viewer README · Installation：Install the plugin into a DeepSeek Harness profile. The plugin does not modify
the `deepseek-harness` repository itself.

```sh

@wangjunjian/dsh-artifact-viewer README · Or from a registry, once published：dsh plugin --profile web add @wangjunjian/dsh-artifact-viewer
```

The bundle is appended to `dsh.profile.bundles` automatically.

@wangjunjian/dsh-artifact-viewer README · Bookmarks file format：Bookmarks are stored in the DeepSeek Harness home under
`~/.dsh/storages/artifact-viewer/bookmarks.json`. The file groups bookmarks by
canonical project path, so multiple projects can share one store while staying
isolated:

